  "_about": "a grey wolf SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-05, gen: scratchpad sc/carn/gen/canids.py): long-legged and narrow-chested over a deep pale brisket, a tucked loin, a sloping croup, big paws; a broad cranium with flared pale cheeks, a long muzzle, short erect ears; countershaded -- a dark saddle and nape, buff flanks, cream legs and belly, a white-lipped mask -- and a bushy dark-tipped tail hanging low || ROUND 2 (2026-11-07, scratchpad var/wlf.py): a canid's wedge skull (broad cranium and cheekbones to a slim muzzle) with a clear stop below the forehead; upright triangular ears; a pale cheek ruff; the legs jointed -- a narrow wrist with the carpal pad's bump, sloped pasterns, toe lobes, the hock's point behind -- and tawny, with the dark line down the front of the foreleg (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): tall pointed cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`), pale in the hollow, the upper edges dark; the roots faired. WHISKERS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sharp/whiskers.py): 12 dark brown whiskers a side, 3 rows on the whisker pad (40-65 mm) -- `whiskers` shapes (bodyspec.js whiskerStrands: thin pointed strands, mirrored, on the head, near mesh only; details, so every coat and variant still shares one mesh). (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/tails.py) The TAIL is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along its bones, not a chain of cones blended one into the next: no beads, its thin end exact rings.",
